0..77 Comment "// State as a theory: `get` passes the state to what runs after it, and `put`"
78..152 Comment "// replaces the state before what runs after it. The laws are the rules of"
153..226 Comment "// global state in Cooper, \"The marriage of effects and rewrites\" (2023),"
227..270 Comment "// § 2.1, each oriented by the path order."
271..273 Comment "//"
274..341 Comment "// A put stores a value: no operation returns the sort `S`, so only"
342..419 Comment "// constructors and variables build a term of it. A continuation instantiated"
420..498 Comment "// at the stored value selects one branch of the abstraction a `get` holds and"
499..576 Comment "// calls no operation, so put-get descends as Cooper\'s branch selection does."
577..654 Comment "// Two of the laws in one theory overlap, and get-get overlaps itself through"
655..715 Comment "// its pattern; each pair joins in the second-order reading."
717..794 Comment "/// The operations alone: reading the state of sort `S` into what runs after,"
795..871 Comment "/// and storing a value of it before what runs after. A handler answers each"
872..920 Comment "/// with the sort fixed (`state-handler.gandr`)."
